{
  "dom_id": "step-q181725",
  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $A=(2,5]?$\n\nThe minimum of the set {{field-1}}, while the maximum of the set {{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nNotice that $2\\notin A.$ So, we have the following:\n\n- $min(A)=min(2,5],$ which $\\text{does not exist}$\n\n- $max(A)=max(2,5]=5$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
